    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_control" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation: explicit control application; machinery readiness is reported separately.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_modules" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation: module planning or reboot. Saving settings alone does not recompile active mappings.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_hide" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation: registration and later binding events. Registered definitions do not prove invisibility.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_maps" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation: explicit managed Maps application. File replacement can require reapplication.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_build" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation: the saved boot stage or an explicitly supported application step.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_phase_unknown" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Activation stage: unknown</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_policy_label" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Policy description — not an observed application result</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_observers_unmeasured" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Ordinary, authorized, root, isolated, shared-UID and work-profile process views have not been measured by this read.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_modules" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Module content uses VIEW or SPOOF according to UID and unmount policy. Isolated/app-zygote targets use SPOOF; non-app UIDs usually use VIEW. A root result cannot verify an ordinary app’s view.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_stealth" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Stealth filters relevant /dev directory entries for SPOOF targets when enabled. It is not the policy used by every hidden path.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_hide" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">User HIDE exempts root, authorized apps and the resolver process. Some storage services also have parent exemptions. This differs from module visibility policy.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_mount" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Filtered mount information applies to isolated targets and non-authorized apps. Privileged/system/authorized tools can retain topology; this is separate from module content visibility.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_maps" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Explicit Maps rules apply to eligible SPOOF targets when enabled. They change Maps rendering and identity, not mapped file contents. Other proxy handling can also apply.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_statfs" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Statfs handling uses mount-view policy and requires statfs and mount hiding to be configured, mount hiding available, and global SUMH enabled. Root/non-root alone is not enough to predict the result.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_build" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Kernel Build modifies initial-UTS strings. It does not use per-application visibility policy and does not rewrite existing cloned UTS namespaces.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_debug" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Kernel debug controls logging machinery. Its active flag is not evidence of any application’s file or mount view.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_xattr" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">Overlay attribute handling filters marked superblocks according to mount-view target policy. Its actual observer effect is not established by the six-control runtime sample.</string>
    <string name="sumh_capabilities_scope_unknown" tools:ignore="MissingTranslation">This read does not establish a process-specific observer policy for this feature.</string>
